CHAPTER.VERS:
And of the Gadites there separated themselves unto David into the hold to the wilderness men of might, [and] men of war [fit] for the battle, that could handle shield and buckler, whose faces [were like] the faces of 

          Meaning, fierce and terrible.
         lions, and [were] as swift as the roes upon the mountains;

And Jehoiada [was] the leader of the 

          Of the Levites who came by the descent of Aaron.
         Aaronites, and with him [were] three thousand and seven hundred;
